    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d145-a1">

                <pb facs="0355" n="259" xml:id="pg259"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 23.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Akerman to Mr. Dichman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Illinois Central Railroad Company, President’s Office</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chicago, Ill.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            25, 1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am very anxious before the next session
                    of Congress, to be able to satisfy some of our Western Congressmen and Senators
                    of the great importance to the West of establishing a line of steamers between
                    New Orleans and South American ports.</p>
                <p>To assist in doing this, I would be obliged to you if you would send me any
                    statistics in your power relative to the trade between the United States of
                    Colombia and this country, and any other information which you may think useful
                    to the end I have in view.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. R. AKERMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
